    {
      "id": "e0f717a6-957e-4990-8c0d-610657e5e4d7",
      "name": "Read me - setup and help",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -820,
        -100
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 720,
        "height": 1150,
        "content": "# Save Google Drive recording transcripts as text files with Palatine Speech\n\n## Who is this for?\nTeams and individuals who accumulate recordings in Drive (calls, memos, lectures) and want each one searchable as text without opening any tool.\n\n## What it does\nDrop recordings into an input Google Drive folder and save their plain-text transcripts into a separate output folder. Palatine Speech handles transcription; a media filter ignores text and other non-media files.\n\n## How it works\n1. **Watch Recordings Folder** \u2014 Google Drive Trigger polls a folder for new files.\n2. **Download Recording** \u2014 downloads the new audio/video file.\n3. **Palatine Speech Transcription** \u2014 converts speech to text (`palatine_large_highspeed`, `$json.transcription`).\n4. **Transcript to .txt File** \u2014 wraps the transcript into a text file named after the recording.\n5. **Save Transcript to Drive** \u2014 uploads `<recording>.txt` back to the same folder.\n\n## Setup\n1. Install community node `n8n-nodes-palatine-speech`, import `workflow.json`.\n2. Attach Google Drive + Palatine Speech credentials.\n3. Pick the folder to watch in the trigger and the same (or another) folder as the upload target.\n4. Activate and drop a recording into the folder.\n\nSelect an input recordings folder and a separate output transcripts folder in Save Transcript to Drive. The media filter also ignores `.txt` files, preventing generated transcripts from triggering repeated transcription.\n\n## Requirements\nInstall the community node `n8n-nodes-palatine-speech` (tested package version 1.1.1). On self-hosted n8n, use Settings \u2192 Community Nodes. On n8n Cloud, use the node picker if the verified package is available to your workspace. Add credentials in n8n; no secrets are included in the template.\n\n## Customization\n- Select a dedicated output folder for transcripts.\n- Add a summary step after transcription.\n- Send the resulting file link to your team.\n\n### Need help with Palatine Speech?\n\nCheck info here: [speech.palatine.ru](https://speech.palatine.ru/)\n\nDocumentation: [docs.speech.palatine.ru](https://docs.speech.palatine.ru/)\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
